# Docker build context exclusions — Docker does NOT read .gitignore, so this
# mirrors it for local `docker build`s (Render builds from a git clone and is
# already protected). Without it, COPY . . (Dockerfile:18) would bake
# mythos/.env (live secrets), vault/ (personal data) and the host's
# node_modules (shadowing the fresh `npm ci` layer) into the image. The
# Dockerfile's "NOT baked into the image" promise for MYTHOS_AUTH_TOKEN is
# enforced here. Pinned by test/deploy-config-conformance.test.js.
#
# Keep-list (runtime reads verified — never ignore these): ui/, skills/ +
# skills.allowlist, personas/, providers/, src/, server/, services/,
# adapters/, mcp/, package*.json. node_modules/ is safe to ignore — npm ci
# runs before COPY . .

# secrets
.env
.env.*

# dependencies — npm ci runs before COPY . .
node_modules/

# local data — real user vault content, never publish
vault/
vault_test_audit_*/

# knowledge-graph build artifact (regenerable via scripts/graphify.js)
.graph-data.json

# fetched model weights — per-machine, never committed (CC BY-NC-SA wake word,
# MIT Silero; see THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md). NOT the whole ui/public/models/ dir:
# gesture_recognizer.task is tracked and runtime-served
# (ui/public/js/vision/camera.js fetches /models/gesture_recognizer.task).
ui/public/models/wakeword/
ui/public/models/silero/
ui/public/models/wakeword.test-backup/

# per-machine TTS/STT model caches (setup-piper/kokoro/whisper scripts)
models/

# tests and their fixtures — not needed in the image
test/
test-fixtures/

# planning / docs / vault-seed content dirs — docs only, no runtime reads
Plans/
docs/
Goals/
Identity/
Semantic/

# e2e run artifacts
scripts/e2e/artifacts/

# session/tooling junk
.browser-agent.pid
.tmp-*
